 following short-term adrenalectomy in the rat: the role of adrenal catecholamines. Behav Neural Biol 39:241&#x02013;258 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6670974</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR5"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Borrell</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Kloet</surname><given-names>ER</given-names></name><name><surname>Bohus</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Corticosterone decreases the efficacy of adrenaline to affect passive avoidance retention of adrenalectomized rats</article-title><source>Life Sci</source><year>1984</year><volume>34</volume><fpage>99</fpage><lpage>104</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1016/0024-3205(84)90336-9</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Borrell J, De Kloet ER, Bohus B (1984) Corticosterone decreases the efficacy of adrenaline to affect passive avoidance retention of adrenalectomized rats. Life Sci 34:99&#x02013;104 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6694514</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR6"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Cabib</surname><given-names>S</given-names></name><name><surname>Orsini</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Moal</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Piazza</surname><given-names>PV</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Abolition and reversal of strain differences in behavioral responses to drugs of abuse after a brief experience</article-title><source>Science</source><year>2000</year><volume>289</volume><fpage>463</fpage><lpage>465</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1126/science.289.5478.463</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Cabib S, Orsini C, Le Moal M, Piazza PV (2000) Abolition and reversal of strain differences in behavioral responses to drugs of abuse after a brief experience. Science 289:463&#x02013;465 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10903209</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR7"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chiueh</surname><given-names>CC</given-names></name><name><surname>Kopin</surname><given-names>IJ</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Centrally mediated release by cocaine of endogenous epinephrine and norepinephrine from the sympathoadrenal medullary system of unanesthetized rats</article-title><source>J Pharmacol Exp Ther</source><year>1978</year><volume>205</volume><fpage>148</fpage><lpage>154</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Chiueh CC, Kopin IJ (1978) Centrally mediated release by cocaine of endogenous epinephrine and norepinephrine from the sympathoadrenal medullary system of unanesthetized rats. J Pharmacol Exp Ther 205:148&#x02013;154 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">633079</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR8"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Darracq</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Blanc</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Glowinski</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><name><surname>Tassin</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Importance of the noradrenaline-dopamine coupling in the locomotor activating effects of <sc>d</sc>-amphetamine</article-title><source>J Neurosci</source><year>1998</year><volume>18</volume><fpage>2729</fpage><lpage>2739</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Darracq L, Blanc G, Glowinski J, Tassin JP (1998) Importance of the noradrenaline-dopamine coupling in the locomotor activating effects of d-amphetamine. J Neurosci 18:2729&#x02013;2739 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">9502830</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR9"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jong</surname><given-names>IEM</given-names></name><name